{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:LiftingAndDescent.JetProlongationCategoricalJet","@type":"LeanModule","name":"LiftingAndDescent.JetProlongationCategoricalJet","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CategoricalFoundations"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.jp_categorical_jet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.jp_categorical_jet","kind":"def","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/jet-prolongation-categorical-jet.lean#L35-L54","doc":"**Categorical jet inherits the ambient category.**\n\nAny `FrobeniusHopfData A` in a monoidal category `C` exhibits\nits underlying object `obj` as a `C`-object — the carrier on\ntop of which the jet construction `J¹(A) := A ⊗ Ω¹(A)` is\nbuilt.  This lemma packages the trivial structural fact that\n`(fhd : FrobeniusHopfData C).obj : C` provides a candidate\ncarrier for the categorical jet inheritance.\n\nThe deeper inheritance of `(Δ', ε', S')` to `J¹(A)` is the\ncontent of the manuscript's §3 construction; the Lean\nformalisation of those structure maps awaits a richer encoding\nof `Ω¹(A)` and the Kähler-differential bimodule. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:lem:jet-prolongation-categorical-jet","label":"lem:jet-prolongation-categorical-jet","md":"quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/jet-prolongation-categorical-jet.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}